ia; NAGLAZYME, a recombinant form of N- acetylgalactosamine 4-sulfatase for patients with MPS VI; and PALYNZIQ, a PEGylated recombinant phenylalanine (Phe) ammonia lyase enzyme delivered through subcutaneous injection to reduce blood Phe concentrations. It also develops BRINEURA, a recombinant human tripeptidyl peptidase 1 for the treatment of patients with ceroid lipofuscinosis type 2, a form of Batten disease; ALDURAZYME, a purified protein designed to be identical to a naturally occurring form of the human enzyme alpha-L-iduronidase; and KUVAN, a proprietary synthetic oral form of 6R-BH4 that is used to treat patients with phenylketonuria, an inherited metabolic disease. The company's products under development include BMN 333, a longer-acting CNP for the treatment of multiple growth disorders, such as achondroplasia and hypochondroplasia; and BMN 351, an oligonucleotide for the treatment of duchenne muscular dystrophy. It serves specialty pharmacies, hospitals, non-U.S. government agencies, distributors, and pharmaceutical wholesalers. The company has license and collaboration agreements with and Ares Trading S.A. The company was incorporated in 1996 and is based in San Rafael, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Alexander  Hardy | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $225K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $56K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["BioMarin Pharmaceutical Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $13.2B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $725M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.37\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 38\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.06844689993860982},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not 